WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.967
You're a student of the game.

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:05.070
If Aaron Judge hits
62 home runs or more,

00:00:05.304 --> 00:00:07.974
is he the authentic
home run champion?

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.079
(CHUCKLES) Oh, man.
That is a very tough question.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.082
I-- You know, I think...
You know, we just touched on it.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.585
Just the history of this game,
there's so much history.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.954
I think it's really hard
to compare eras.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:25.891
And that Barry Bonds era
is a unique distinction
in this game.

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.595
The Roger Maris before that
was a different time as well.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.997
I mean, you put Roger Maris
into today's game,

00:00:32.097 --> 00:00:33.732
or Babe Ruth in today's game

00:00:33.832 --> 00:00:35.067
with everybody coming out
of the bull pen,

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.101
throwing 100 miles an hour,

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:37.770
you know, who knows what
they're able to accomplish?

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.939
So I think we need
to really appreciate

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.042
what Judge is doing right now
in this era, on his own.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:45.578
I mean, it's...
I think it's...

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.081
You know, I think there's
two separate numbers, though.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.251
You know, there's Roger's
and there's Barry's.

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:57.489
And I think
to be able to reach Maris',
I think, should be celebrated

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:02.695
because the '90s era was just
a different era of baseball.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:03.796
It's live ball.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.932
You have a live-ball era,
a dead-ball era, a steroid era,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.466
whatever era it is.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.603
But it's really fun to see
what he's able to do,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.206
and bring attention
to this game.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.407
You know,
that's what it's all about.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.709
So I can't really answer
that question,

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.211
but I think it should
definitely be celebrated

00:01:19.311 --> 00:01:21.548
if he passes Maris' record.

